  "behavior": [
    "EVM signing context now captures the selected network.currentProvider configuration, so a persistent RPC configuration change invalidates the queued review.",
    "Local transactions use ethers VoidSigner to populate nonce, gas, fee and chain fields without accessing a private key. Authorization and captured request/provider identity are revalidated after the initial provider-chain query and unsigned population.",
    "Detached Wallet signing is followed by fresh authorization validation and a synchronous request/provider-instance check before provider.broadcastTransaction. The signed chain and original JSON-RPC gas limit are verified by decoding real transaction bytes.",
    "Local message and typed-data signatures are revalidated before release. A mobile result returned after a persistent authorization change is rejected and its intent consumed.",
    "Pre-submission failures leave the exact local request rejectable; ambiguous broadcast failures consume it so the same screen cannot retry with a fresh nonce. Existing pending and one-shot request ownership remains intact."
  ],
